# Normalise line endings.
#
# This repository is authored on both Windows and Linux and deployed to Linux. A shell
# script or Dockerfile that reaches the server with CRLF line endings fails in a way that
# reads like a missing file: the kernel treats the shebang as `/usr/bin/env bash\r`, which
# does not exist, and reports "command not found" for a script that is plainly there.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Files that must never be converted.
*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile    text eol=lf
Caddyfile       text eol=lf
*.conf          text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf

# Binary — never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary

# Generated; keep diffs collapsed in review.
pnpm-lock.yaml -diff linguist-generated
